Z||000000||stsmithgt||08-18-99||05:33 PM||||I have a pretty consistant problem.  I travel down the freeway for a considerable amount of time and then pull off the freeway to only get stopped at a street light.  At the time the light turns green and I attempt to leave, my car acts like it's running out of gas.  I first jumped to the conclusion that I had a vapor lock problem, but maybe it's a sensor giving the wrong info. It seems to have something to do with the heat build up under the hood from running it down the freeway.  That's the only time it's ever had this symtom.  Pulling over and letting it cool down turned off or idleing stops the problem.  I would like to eliminate the problem entirely.  If anyone knows a possible solution, I would be gratefull.
